getMergedSymbol tests a bit of the symbol's id before it asks the table

getMergedSymbol runs for every symbol a check touches. Symbols of a shared program have their
ids from creation, so each call looked the id up in mergedSymbols, a Map<number, Symbol> that
holds the few symbols the program merges: nearly every lookup hashed the id and found nothing
(2.9% of the samples of the checker that checks checker.ts of the TypeScript compiler project,
garnet build). The checker keeps one bit per id that is or has been a key of the table; a clear
bit answers without the lookup. The bits are a superset of the keys: they are set where a
checker takes its table (its own, a copy, or the library globals it borrows) and by
setMergedSymbol, the one writer; an undo of a borrowed table leaves them set.

